              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>In a region famous for waterfalls, Looking Glass Falls might be the closest thing N.C. has to a hometown celebrity. Located just off U.S. 276 in Pisgah National Forest, this 60-foot cascade delivers one of the biggest payoffs in the Blue Ridge for one of the smallest investments. A short staircase leads from the parking area to the base, where Looking Glass Creek fans across a broad rock face before crashing into a chilly pool below. I might be biased because it’s close to home, but if you've only got time for one waterfall in Appalachia, this is a strong contender.</p></div>
